{
  "Documentation": [
    "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_s3.html",
    "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_s3_syntax.html",
    "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/access-control-block-public-access.html"
  ],
  "EvidenceClass": "documented-contract-local-replay-not-native-write-capture",
  "Notes": [
    "All replay writes target the local retainedCloud server. Separate native admission captures created and removed unattached policy definitions without changing account protections, attachments, enabled policy types or memberships.",
    "One root-attached policy exercises real Organizations publication into S3Control and ordinary S3; generated root and policy identifiers are rebound from SDK responses.",
    "ManualTime and Advance run existing scheduled jobs deterministically on memory and retained SQLite. The one-second publication boundary is the local service model, not a measured AWS propagation SLA.",
    "The distinct stored RestrictPublicBuckets setting must survive all and none, rejected writes, policy update, detach, disable, and retained reopen. Organization none overrides account settings but not bucket restrictions or ordinary IAM denial.",
    "An attached partial policy with no assignment uses the existing declarative inheritance grammar: once its empty effective view publishes, retained account settings apply again."
  ],
  "RemainingNativeGaps": [
    "No native S3_POLICY attachment, detachment, enable/disable, propagation or account override writes were performed. Unattached create/update admission is captured separately in s3_policy_admission_evidence.json.gz.",
    "This concentrated replay covers root inheritance; OU conflicts, new-member inheritance, and SCP interactions are not asserted here."
  ],
